{"name":"Antler Velvet","hex":"#c0ad96","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"antler","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous branching and bony structure on the head of deer (Cervidae), normally in pairs, grown and shed each year."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antler"},{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antler","blocks":[{"text":"Antlers are extensions of an animal's skull found in members of the Cervidae (deer) family. Antlers are a single structure composed of bone, cartilage, fibrous tissue, skin, nerves, and blood vessels. They are generally found only on males, with the exception of reindeer/caribou. Antlers are shed and regrown each year and function primarily as objects of sexual attraction and as weapons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Red_deer_stag_2009_denmark.jpg/330px-Red_deer_stag_2009_denmark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antler"},{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg/500px-Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg/500px-Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red deer at the beginning of the growing season","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/KaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg/500px-KaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/KaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg/1280px-KaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/KaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg/500px-KaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male fallow deer fighting","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKaempfendeHirsche-2-cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Sambar_deers_Fighting_Silvassa.jpg/500px-Sambar_deers_Fighting_Silvassa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Sambar_deers_Fighting_Silvassa.jpg/1280px-Sambar_deers_Fighting_Silvassa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna